只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"【EMNLP 2026 Demo】A debugging framework for agentic AI systems: diagnose failures, attribute root causes, recover with evidence, and validate fixes through reruns.","id":"gh:1296792947","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"AgentDebugX","slug":"AgentDebugX/AgentDebugX","topics":["agent-debugging","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"【EMNLP 2026 Demo】A debugging framework for agentic AI systems: diagnose failures, attribute root cau"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ses, recover with evidence, and validate fixes through reruns."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# AgentDebugX"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**A local-first debugging framework for agentic AI systems: diagnose failures, attribute root causes"},{"id":"p3s2","text":", recover with evidence, and validate fixes through reruns.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"AgentDebugX turns failed agent runs into structured, auditable debugging\nartifacts. It ingests a liv"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"e or exported trajectory, detects visible failure\nsignals, attributes them to responsible steps or a"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"gents, proposes recovery\nactions, and prepares controlled reruns so fixes can be validated instead o"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"poses recovery\nactions, and prepares controlled reruns so fixes can be validated instead of\nguessed."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"The project is designed for researchers and engineers building complex LLM\nagents: multi-agent syste"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ms, tool-using agents, computer-use agents, benchmark\nrunners, and local agent development workflows"},{"id":"p5s3","text":". AgentDebugX is local-first by\ndefault: traces stay on your machine, sharing is opt-in, and recover"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"y proposals\ncarry explicit policy and approval metadata into the Rerun boundary."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## 📰 News"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- 🔌 **2026-08-25** — Released\n`dsh-agentdebugx` v0.1.0,\nthe AgentDebugX plugin for DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p7s2","text":"\n- 📄 **2026-07-31** — Released\nCUADebug, our framework for diagnosing\nand repairing computer-use age"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"nt failures.\n- 📄 **2026-07-21** — Released the\nAgentDebugX paper, presenting our\nopen-source toolkit"},{"id":"p7s4","text":" for failure observability, attribution, recovery, and\nrerun in LLM agents.\n- 📦 **2026-05-16** — Rel"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"eased AgentDebugX on\nPyPI.\n- 📄 **2025-09-29** — Released\nWhere LLM Agents Fail and How They Can Lear"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"n From Failures,\nintroducing AgentErrorTaxonomy, AgentErrorBench, and AgentDebug."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## System Overview"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"AgentDebugX follows the two-stage loop used by the project paper:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"`Diagnose` explains what failed and why. `Rerun` tests whether the proposed\nrecovery actually improv"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"es the agent behavior."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Why AgentDebugX"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Tracing tools show what happened. AgentDebugX focuses on the debugging step that\nusually comes next:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- Which earlier decision caused the visible failure?\n- Which agent, tool call, memory read, handoff,"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" or GUI action was responsible?\n- What evidence supports that diagnosis?\n- What concrete recovery sh"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ould be tried?\n- Did the rerun branch improve the outcome?"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The output is a portable diagnostic report that can be inspected in a local UI,\nused by a CLI workfl"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ow, stored in an Error Hub bundle, or invoked from an\nagentic skill."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Core Capabilities"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- **Portable trace schema**: framework-agnostic trajectory, event, finding, and\ndiagnostic report mo"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"dels.\n- **Ingest adapters**: normalize raw JSON, LangGraph, CrewAI, OpenAI Agents SDK,\nOpenTelemetry"},{"id":"p17s3","text":", GAIA/Open Deep Research, OSWorld, and other exported traces.\n- **Detect**: deterministic analyzers"},{"id":"p17s4","text":", manifest-backed rule packs, LLM judge\nmode, GUI-aware signals, and taxonomy induction support.\n- *"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"*Attribute**: heuristic attribution, all-at-once analysis, step-by-step\nlocalization, binary search,"},{"id":"p17s6","text":" counterfactual attribution, MOE localization,\nand DeepDebug.\n- **Recover**: Reflexion, CRITIC, Self"},{"id":"p17s7","text":"-Refine, AutoManual, DeepDebug recovery,\nand saga rollback style strategies.\n- **Rerun**: three expl"},{"id":"p17s8","text":"icit modes for plan/export only, labeled simulation, or\nobserved execution in an application-owned p"},{"id":"p17s9","text":"rocess or persistent HTTP runner.\n- **Local inspection UI**: no-build FastAPI dashboard for traces, "},{"id":"p17s10","text":"reports,\nbefore/after CUA visuals, debugger discussions, saved cases, debug branches,\nand rerun-from"},{"id":"p17s11","text":"-event workflows.\n- **Error Hub**: scrubbed, shareable failure bundles for regression tests,\nbenchma"},{"id":"p17s12","text":"rk corpora, and team debugging memory.\n- **Agent integrations**: generate host-runtime assets such a"},{"id":"p17s13","text":"s debugging skills\nfor external agent tools."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Optional extras:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Computer-use / OSWorld GUI root-cause analysis (`agentdebug.gui`) ships with the\ncore install and ne"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"eds no extra. The `gui` extra only adds `pillow`, which the\nRCA tools use to decode screenshots. Two"},{"id":"p22s3","text":" heavier layers of the same package sit\nbehind their own extras: `gui-memory` for the lesson/episodi"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"c memory stack, and\n`gui-app` for the provider adapters, the batch pipeline (`python -m\nagentdebug.g"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"ui`) and the Streamlit annotation app."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"The package is installed as `agentdebugx` and imported as `agentdebug`:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Claude Code and Codex Plugins"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"AgentDebugX ships native plugins for Claude Code and Codex so an agent can\ndebug its own session. Th"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"e plugin bundles capture hooks and the AgentDebug\nskill, which keeps two boundaries explicit:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- **Capture is automatic** once a project opts in. Sessions are normalized into\nAgentDebugX trajecto"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ries locally and silently.\n- **Diagnosis is explicit.** Ask AgentDebug in-session and the skill diag"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"noses\nthat exact captured trajectory with `agentdebug run --current --profile deep`.\nRe-running or r"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"epairing the agent's work stays a separately authorized step."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Follow the capture quickstart to install a plugin,\nenable project capture, diagnose a session, and t"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"urn capture off again."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The plugin bundles live in this repository:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| Plugin | Bundle | Documentation |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"The repository mirrors the paper-level workflow:"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Detailed references:"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"- Architecture\n- Trace schema\n- System overview PDF"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Privacy and Safety"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"AgentDebugX is local-first:"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"- Trace capture and diagnosis run locally unless you explicitly configure an\nexternal LLM endpoint.\n"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"- Error Hub publishing is opt-in.\n- Bundle scrubbing is available before sharing traces.\n- Recovery "},{"id":"p39s3","text":"is suggest-only. External execution belongs to Rerun and requires an\nexplicitly configured executor."},{"id":"p39s4","text":" Recovery approval fields are auditable\nmetadata; deployments must enforce their own authorization p"},{"id":"p39s5","text":"olicy before\ndispatch."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"Diagnostic findings are hypotheses with evidence and provenance, not ground\ntruth. LLM Judge reports"},{"id":"p40s2","text":" retain the model's self-reported confidence;\nHeuristic and DeepDebug reports omit uncalibrated conf"},{"id":"p40s3","text":"idence values. Configure\nretention, access control, and redaction before collecting production trace"},{"id":"p40s4","text":"ence values. Configure\nretention, access control, and redaction before collecting production traces."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
